      "source_scope": "W01 §3.1 eqs. 3.1-3.2",
      "exact_frozen_census_body": "W01's frame-bundle description distinguishes spin-connection one-forms omega from canonical/frame one-forms e, takes e and omega as the fundamental Palatini fields, and writes the action as the integral of epsilon_ABCD e^A wedge e^B wedge Omega^CD(omega); its equations of motion are obtained by varying omega^AB, which gives de^A + omega^A_B wedge e^B = 0 and thereby the torsion-free Levi-Civita connection determined by e, and by varying e^A, which gives the Einstein equations in terms of e. Its printed source action is precisely integral_M epsilon_ABCD e^A wedge e^B wedge Omega^CD(omega), where Omega(omega) denotes curvature of the spin connection, not an independent arbitrary field. Varying omega^AB gives the source-printed torsion equation de^A+omega^A_B wedge e^B=0; varying e^A separately gives Einstein equations. No generic zero-stationarity operator or variation-direction carrier is claimed.",
